A thread without time waits on the run queue all the same.
It takes turns before the threads on spare time, and one held to its units is not;
a ready thread waits on the queue its account and binding say.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a thread waits on another queue than its account says

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -189,10 +189,7 @@ static uint8_t thread_queue(const struct thread *t, uint32_t balance)
     if (has_time(balance)) {
         return QUEUE_RUN;
     }
-    if (thread_spare(t)) {
-        return QUEUE_SPARE;
-    }
-    return thread_units(t) != 0 ? QUEUE_SPENT : QUEUE_NONE;
+    return QUEUE_RUN;
 }
 
